Does anyone else wonder about the circumstances of a character's death
when you load a bones level from Hearse (or on a public server)?  I got
an interesting one the other day, and was wondering if someone here
might step up and claim it.

I got to DL15, and encountered a named gray elf.  I don't recall the
name, but it was long, with a first and last name and middle initial.
Then I killed an invisible monster that dropped a longsword and shield.
 Then I found the ghost of Dread, who was killed by an invisible aleax.
 There was also a chaotic altar on the level.

The thing I thought was odd was the contents of the bones pile.  There
were a lot of rings, wands, and spell books, but the armor was nothing
to write home about - speed boots, mithril I think, maybe 1 or 2 other
pieces - and the weapon sucked (just a staff, iirc).  I couldn't ID
everything on the spot, so the stash got combined with my own, but I do
know that one of the wands was later IDed as a /oW (0:0).

My theory:  Dread was probably a spellcaster - a healer, or perhaps a
priest.  He was shuttling equipment from 1 stash to another.  With no
bag, he carried only the minimum regular equipment thought necessary,
but that wasn't enough, and he got caught with his pants down by the
Aleax.  But he had a used /oW...  If you're not adverse to using
wishes, why was there no DSM or BoH?  Perhaps he was going wishless and
wished for "nothing" when he engrave-tested an unknown wand.  Or maybe
he just wished for speed boots instead of ?oChargings, and the wand
turned out to have just 1 charge.

So can anyone here claim Dread and his pet gray elf, and shed some
light on the circumstances here?  Enquiring minds want to know! :)
Either way, thanks for the =oSD!



